[sliver] Set aside by Derek, not accepted: these six faces bound the 1.35 mm pockets the outer fore valves' coil yokes need in the flank. Flattening the flank needs those valves 1.35 mm inboard, which puts their upper tubes, or with the tees moved their pump tubes, 1.35 mm off straight and pushing on the tee and cartridge. Derek: "I don't love it. But it's not the highest priority problem."
alternatives: Move the outer fore valves 1.35 mm inboard and accept the bent upper tube, or move valve and tee together and accept the bent pump tube. Thinning the whole flank to the pocket floor drags the seam-rail and funnel-frame grooves outboard.
